    {
      "name": "Auth - Google",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Google Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "if (res && res.data && res.data.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", res.data.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", res.data.refreshToken || \"\");",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"idToken\": \"<google-id-token-from-frontend-sign-in>\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/google",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "google"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**, returning the app's own `accessToken`/`refreshToken` (body + cookies).\n\nResolution order: (1) known `googleId` (matched by the stable `sub` claim), (2) an existing account with the same email gets linked (`googleId` set, `emailVerified` forced true; an existing password is preserved), (3) otherwise a new `PATIENT` user + `Patient` row is provisioned.\n\n`idToken` must be a real Google ID token verified against `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` — see `GOOGLE-LOGIN-TESTING.md` in the repo for how to obtain one for manual testing."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "ID-token verification only. The frontend runs Google Sign-In, gets an ID token, and POSTs it here; the server verifies it and issues its own JWTs. Google is never involved again after this call."
    },
